---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../site.config.ts';
const updated = 'October 21, 2026';
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy" description="How Newspaper Front Page Maker handles your photos, text, cookies and ads. Your photo stays on your device and is never uploaded. No sign-up is needed.">
  <p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
  <p>This policy explains what {site.name} ({site.domain}) collects and why.</p>
  <h2>What the tool does with your input</h2>
  <p>The tool runs in your browser. The photos you add are read and drawn on your device. The page does not send your photos or your text to our servers or to anyone else. You can check this in the Network tab of your browser tools. When you download a page, the file is made on your device. If you use Copy link, your words and settings are put in the link itself, after the # sign. Browsers do not send that part to any server, but anyone you give the link to can read the words. Photos are never put in a link.</p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We do not ask you to create an account. We do not collect names or email addresses, unless you email us. If you do, we use your address only to reply.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>We may use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people use. Google Analytics sets cookies and collects data such as your IP address, browser, device and pages viewed. We use this data in aggregate to improve the site. Learn how Google uses data in its <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">"How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services"</a> page. You can block the tracking with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p>
  <h2>Advertising and third-party vendors</h2>
  <p>We may show ads from Google AdSense and other third-party vendors. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your earlier visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and its partners serve ads to you based on your visit to our site and other sites on the internet.</p>
  <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> to opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising.</p>
  <p>When ads or analytics are on, consent is shown through Google's consent message. You can also change your choice in your browser settings or by clearing cookies. This site has no cookie banner of its own.</p>
  <h2>Your browser's local storage</h2>
  <p>The site saves two things in your browser: your light or dark theme choice, and your front page text and settings (layout, size, look), so a reload does not lose your work. This stays on your device. We cannot see it. Photos are never saved: they stay in the open tab only. Use Start over in the tool, or clear your browser data, to remove the saved text.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The site is not aimed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect their data.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what data we hold, and to ask us to correct or delete it. Write to <a href={site.contactHref}>{site.contactLabel}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy. The date above shows the latest update.</p>
</Page>
